<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37743" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-mĭnistro</span></b> ,
		āre, v. n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, <i>to wait</i> or <i>attend upon</i>, <i>to minister
			to</i> any one (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">magistratibus,</span>”
				<i>of the lictors</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					12, 3, 3</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. 10, 3, 13</span></i>: alicui,
			
			<i><span class="en">App. M. 5, p. 160,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to furnish</i>, <i>supply</i>, <i>hand to</i> any one: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ac praeministrasse modulos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 1, 11, 10</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tert. Bapt. 11</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fabulas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Apol. 21</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
